 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? The seat height should be such that the tops of the seat tube and the bottom bracket are roughly the same height. No worries. When you pedal normally, the bottom bracket shouldn't rise more than about three or four centimetres. That's usually because the seat post is too high. Lowering it even a little will usually fix the pain. You should still be able to touch the ground with your heel. If you can't, your seat is too low and you' strain your hamstrings.",
